// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`root help > snapshots the default root help output 1`] = `
"🔨 mjölnir — verification trust engine for test suites and CI pipelines

Usage: mjolnir [path] [options] · mjolnir <subcommand> [args] · mjolnir help <verb>

The product is one command in CI:

  mjolnir --scope changed        scan only what the branch touched; exit 1 on
                                 new findings. \`mjolnir ci install\` writes the
                                 workflow for you.

Everything else is optional.

  mjolnir [path]                 full-repo scan + WORTHINESS score
  mjolnir explain <RULE-ID>      what/why/fix + measured FP rate for one rule
  mjolnir rules --unmeasured     the rules running on assumption, not measurement

Options:
  --json                  machine-readable output
  --format sarif          SARIF 2.1 for GitHub Code Scanning
  --format codequality    GitLab Code Quality report (MR widget artifact)
  --format mermaid        test-architecture diagram
  --tone blunt            blunter, pattern-mocking messages
  --verbose               show all findings
  --scope changed         only new/changed lines vs merge-base
  --max-duration <sec>    analysis time budget
  --width <cols>          override terminal width
  --ascii / --no-ascii    force glyph mode
  --strict                include quarantine-tier rules
  --debug                 print swallowed rule crashes
  --cache                 reuse local per-file verdicts
  --no-progress           no live scan-progress line on stderr
  --score                 print only the numeric score (or \`unknown\`)
  --category <cat>        presentation filter (repeatable)
  --staged                scan only git staged files
  --blocking <level>      exit-status override: error|warning|none
  --enable-plugins        allow npm/JS-module rules (default OFF)
  -v, --version           print the installed version and exit
  -h, --help              show this help

Subcommands — Scan:

Subcommands — CI & PRs:
  ci install [--gate advisory|error|warning] [--no-action] [--force]
    generate the PR workflow (action-based by default; scan + annotations + gate)
  summary [mjolnir.json] [--stdout] [--path-prefix <dir>]
    CI annotations + step summary from a saved --json report
  pr-comment [path] [--base <ref>]                render a scoped PR comment (Markdown)
  badge [path]                                    shields.io endpoint JSON + snippet
                                                  from a scan
  trust-report [path]                             deterministic, self-contained Trust
                                                  Artifact (md + json)
  impact [path] [--since <ref>]                   what a commit introduced vs resolved,
                                                  since a prior commit
  baseline [path]                                 snapshot the current finding set as
                                                  the comparison point
  diff [path] [--json] [scan flags]               lifecycle diff vs the committed
                                                  baseline
  verify [path] [--json] [scan flags]             agent-loop digest:
                                                  resolved/new/unchanged vs baseline +
                                                  score delta
  ci-integrity [path] [--json]                    verify CI workflow integrity and
                                                  suppression governance

Subcommands — Forensics:
  forensics <test-results-dir-or-report-file> [--no-flaky-md]
    runtime evidence from a real run: retries, flakes, durations
  triage <test-results-dir-or-report-file> [--no-md]
    flaky-triage proposal + TRIAGE.md meeting artifact
  pw-report <playwright-report.json | test-results-dir>
    Playwright run summary (counts, true flakes, slowest tests)
  doctor:playwright [path]                        Playwright deep scan + Selector Health
                                                  report

Subcommands — Mutation evidence:
  mutation <mutation-report> [--scan .]           mutation-evidence reader:
                                                  survived-mutant leaderboard + E1→E2
                                                  derivation

Subcommands — Maintenance:
  fix [path] [--dry-run]                          apply safe auto-fixes with proof
                                                  (re-scan verifies each)
  debt [path]                                     test-debt register with an estimated
                                                  quarterly cost
  stats                                           all-time local counters of fixes seen
                                                  via diff
  suppressions                                    list suppressed findings (governance
                                                  transparency)
  handover [path]                                 new-QA onboarding map of the suite
  init [--interactive]                            detect frameworks + setup checklist
                                                  (never overwrites)
  doctor [repo-root]                              self-audit of the rule base (fixture
                                                  firewall, tiers, caps)
  release-trust [--json] [repo-root]              Release Trust Verdict over the
                                                  canonical 12 dimensions
                                                  (docs/RELEASE-TRUST-CONTRACT.md)
  create-rule <QA-XXX-nnn> --title "Rule title"   scaffold a new rule + fixtures
                                                  (must-fire, must-not-fire)
  cross-file [path] [--json]                      analyze cross-file signals:
                                                  duplicates, shared imports, circular
                                                  deps
  contract-verify [path] [--json]                 verify machine contract integrity
                                                  against scan results
  trust-trend [path] [--json]                     track historical trust trends and
                                                  detect regressions
  evidence-graph [path] [--json]                  build and query the verification
                                                  evidence graph
  framework-maturity [--framework <name>]         track framework maturity levels,
                                                  especially Playwright F4→F6
  suppression-gate [path] [--policy <file>]       enforce suppression policy governance
                                                  gate

Subcommands — Meta:
  rules [--md] [--unmeasured|--measured] [--external] | [--stats] | [--health]
  [--limit=N]
    rule catalog + empirical-measurement stats/health (md/json/stats/health)
  explain <RULE-ID> [--fixtures-root <dir>]       what/why/fix + measured FP rate for
                                                  one rule
  why <file>:<line> [path] [--json <mjolnir.json>]
    why did Mjölnir flag <file>:<line>? evidence + fix (not a gate)
  handoff [mjolnir.json] [--category <cat>] [--rules <ids>]
    deterministic fix-handoff artifact from a saved --json report
  install [--staged-hook] [--dry-run] [--force]   install the agent instruction surfaces
                                                  + optional staged hook
  mcp                                             run as an MCP server over stdio (scan
                                                  / explain / diff / verify tools)

Copy-paste starts:
  $ mjolnir                         score this repo's test suite
  $ mjolnir --scope changed         CI gate: only what the branch touched
  $ mjolnir ci install              write the PR workflow
  $ mjolnir forensics test-results  where the flakes hide

Per-command help: mjolnir help <verb>   (e.g. mjolnir help fix)

Exit codes: 0 · 1 · 2 · 10 · 20
  0   clean — no findings or the requested artifact was produced
  1   errors found (or the diff/impact verdict says the PR should not merge)
  2   partial — the scan ran but was truncated, or input was unreadable
  10  usage — bad flags or arguments; help is printed
  20  crash — internal error; rerun with --debug for the stack trace

Docs: https://github.com/Sergey-Bar/Mjolnir#readme   (JSON schemaVersion 1, additive-only)"
`;

